# Portal shell ownership (no double nav)

## Rule

Authenticated PathEd chrome (header + sidebar + main frame) has **exactly one owner**:

`src/app/(app)/(portal)/layout.tsx` → `<PortalShell>`

## Do

- Put page UI only in `src/views/Platform/*` and route `page.tsx` loaders
- Nested layouts under `(portal)/dashboard` must pass `children` through unchanged
- Reuse feature components inside `<main>` content only

## Do not

- Import or render `PortalShell`, `DashboardLayout`, `AppNavbar`, or `DashboardSidebar` from:
  - `src/views/**`
  - any `page.tsx`
  - nested dashboard layouts
- Wrap a view in a second full-page shell (`min-h-screen` + header clone)

## Why

Mounting chrome twice creates the double-nav bug. App Router layouts own shells; pages own content. This matches Next.js App Router industry practice.
